# MI-PATCHES -- every deliberate divergence of src/cc from the pristine MWC
# 4.2.12 donor, with the argument that justifies it.  Read by
# tests/mi-divergence.py (`make check-mi', which `make check' runs); the BAKED
# table in docs/PATCHES.md is RENDERED from this file by `make mi-table' and is
# not the record.
#
# One record per fix, blank-line separated:
#
#	patch: <id>
#	file:  <path> [<sha256 of that file as this justification was written>]
#	fix:   what the edit does
#	why:   why it is correct ON THE NATIVE C900 -- int is 16 bits, K&R, a
#	       segmented Z8001 -- not merely why it builds on the host
#
# The hash is required for every machine-INDEPENDENT file (a machine-layer file
# named by a fix that spans both sides carries none, since that side of the tree
# is ours to change).  It is what stops this from being prose: a file cannot be
# excused by naming it, only by naming it at a stated content, so a second,
# unrelated edit to an already-patched file fails the gate until somebody
# re-reads the argument against the new text.  That is not hypothetical -- it is
# how n1/sel0.c came to carry an undocumented change under a row about something
# else.
#
# `fix' and `why' are continued by repeating the field; the lines are joined
# with a space.

